{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["And Lavan came into the tent of Ya'akov — and afterwards into the tent of Leah, and afterwards into the tent of the two maidservants. And why did he not find them in the tent of Rachel? Because when he went out from the tent of Leah and came into the tent of Rachel, Rachel was sitting on the camel's saddle in which the terafim were hidden." "And he went out from the tent of Leah and came into the tent of Rachel — that is: even though we said above 'into the tent of Leah' and 'into the tent of the two maidservants,' it was not so. Rather, at first, when he went out from the tent of Leah, he entered the tent of Rachel. But on account of the length of the words that Lavan spoke to Rachel and Rachel to Lavan, he did not want to interrupt the first verse."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:55.758287524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}